ALGORITHM

DefectiveCoin(A, low, high)

1. If low == high
      return low

2. If number of coins is even
      Divide into two equal groups
      Weigh both groups

      If weights are equal
          return NONE

      If left group is lighter
          search left group
      Else
          search right group

3. If number of coins is odd
      Keep one coin aside
      Divide remaining coins into two equal groups
      Weigh both groups

      If one group is lighter
          search lighter group

      If both groups are equal
          compare remaining coin with a known good coin
          if lighter → defective
          else → NONE

Complexity

Each step approximately halves the number of coins:

T(n)=T(n/2)+O(1)

Therefore:

T(n)=O(log₂ n )+ c
which satisfies the required log₂ n + c form.
